  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "the \"A\" phase of the 13kV Voltage Regulator shorted to ground through the Current Transformer (CT) secondary wiring due to insufficient clearance. Inadequate work practices lead to insufficient clearance between the installed CT wire and the live 13kV bus bar. The CT wire was routed too close to the bus bar such that induced heat allowed the wire to sag and contact the 13kV bus bar.",
    "cause_code": "B",
    "category": "Design/Manufacturing/Installation",
    "theme": "inadequate clearance/installation of CT secondary wiring near energized bus bar",
    "provisional": false
  },
