  "chain": "inadequate work practices / insufficient clearance [cause B] -> CT wire sagged from induced heat -> contacted energized 13kV bus bar -> phase A shorted to ground -> differential relay tripped feeder breaker, isolating U-4000-22 transformer -> loss of 22/23/24 4kV buses -> loss of CEDM MG sets -> reactor trip bus undervoltage -> automatic reactor trip (scram) [backups: AFW manually initiated, 2B EDG auto-started, alternate breakers restored buses]",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Loss of 22/23 4kV NSR buses also independently caused trip of Condensate/Condensate Booster pumps and Main Feedwater, modeled as a parallel branch (fm_mfw_trip) off fm_bus_loss, not merged with the CEDM MG set loss branch. AFW was manually initiated in response (not an automatic safety-system actuation) but is stated as available/operable during the event, satisfying BACKED_UP_BY criteria. The 2B EDG auto-started and restored the 24 4kV SR bus, also modeled as a stated-operable backup. No PART_OF edge from breaker to transformer (functional/power relationship). Previous-occurrence review found no prior similar events, so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge emitted per rule 9's conditionality."
